All 12 tests passed. Here's what was changed:

**`app/auth.py`** — Implemented `require_api_key`: reads `X-API-Key` header, looks it up in `VALID_API_KEYS`, returns the username on match, raises HTTP 401 with distinct messages for missing vs. invalid keys.

**`app/main.py`** — Added five new features:

| Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|
| `GET /tasks?status=&priority=&assigned_to=&page=&page_size=` | Filtering (status, priority, assigned_to — all optional, combinable) + pagination (page defaults to 1, page_size to 20, capped at 100) |
| `POST /tasks` | Auth required, validates project_id exists (404 if not), auto-generates integer ID via `max()`, returns 201 |
| `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` | Auth required, partial update via `model_copy(update=...)` with `exclude_unset=True`, returns 404 if not found |
| `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` | Auth required, returns 204 on success, 404 if not found |
| — | Unauthenticated requests to any mutating endpoint return 401 ("Missing API key" or "Invalid API key") |
